            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Sanskrit for puts to use, then the Sanskrit for a handing out."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: जहाति",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "जहाति — jahāti — \"leaves behind; abandons\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "यदि सः आलस्यं जहाति, तर्हि सः सुखी भविष्यति। yadi saḥ ālasyaṃ jahāti, tarhi saḥ sukhī bhaviṣyati. If he leaves laziness behind, he will be happy."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (he …): सः गृहं हीनवान्, saḥ gṛhaṃ hīnavān."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "जहाति (jahāti) comes from the root √hā, \"to leave, to abandon\", whose present is jahāti; its past participle is hīna (MW)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for saying what happens if."
            }
          ]
        },
